  "story": "Towers of different heights stand side by side along a street, each one block wide. After heavy rain, water stays in every dip that has a taller tower somewhere on both sides, and runs off at the two open ends of the street. How many blocks of water stay? The gauge can remember only a handful of numbers, not a second list as long as the street, and looking left and right from every tower is too slow.",
