  "hints": ["The water above a tower rises to the lower of two heights: the tallest tower to its left and the tallest to its right.", "Keep one mark at each end and the tallest tower seen so far from each end. Look at the two towers under the marks: the lower one can be settled now, because the other side is known to hold something at least as tall.", "Move the mark under the lower tower inward. IF that tower is at least as tall as the tallest seen on its side, it becomes the new tallest; ELSE add the difference to the water."],
